/E (The fuel type analysis shows that Hybrids lead the used car market, outperforming both Petrol and Electric vehicles. This indicates that hybrid cars are gaining strong popularity in the secondhand market, likely due to their balance between fuel efficiency and affordability compared to fully electric models. Petrol cars still hold a solid share, reflecting their wide availability and established presence. Interestingly, Electric vehicles lag behind hybrids in the used market, which may be due to higher initial purchase prices, limited charging infrastructure in some regions, or concerns about battery life over time. Diesel cars represent the smallest portion, consistent with the global shift away from diesel technology..)
